The desk marked #4471 known as one date bug. Its export contains overlapping pages, so count
each report ID once. The cause depends on the tenant's locale, booking form, and intake channel;
the intake tag is only a guess.

## Reports by cause

<Callout>
The component deduplicates report IDs before counting. The two causes in #4471 have separate
follow-up issues: [the shared parser](https://github.com/filipzinowiew-allegro/megadev/issues/2)
and [the booking-v3 form hint](https://github.com/filipzinowiew-allegro/megadev/issues/1).
</Callout>

<CauseTable ticket={4471} issues={issues} />

## Why these are separate

- **Shared parser.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenant dates flip.
  This cause covers app and email reports, booking-v2 form reports, and booking-v3 reports not
  submitted through its form. See [issue #2](https://github.com/filipzinowiew-allegro/megadev/issues/2).
- **booking-v3 form hint.** The form shows `MM/DD/YYYY`, but day-first tenants' form submissions
  are read in tenant order. People follow the hint, so month and day flip. See
  [issue #1](https://github.com/filipzinowiew-allegro/megadev/issues/1).

